---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="How Anchor handles family chat data, media, and AI processing for the Athina prototype."
  currentPath="/privacy"
>
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Anchor is a hackathon prototype. This page explains what the demo collects and how it is used.
    </p>

    <h2>What we process</h2>
    <p>
      When you use the web demo or connect WhatsApp via Twilio, Anchor may process message text, photos, and voice notes
      you send so it can store family moments and run spaced-retrieval practice.
    </p>

    <h2>Why</h2>
    <p>
      Content is sent to Google Gemini to extract a recallable moment (who, what, when, a practice question) and optionally
      to synthesise speech. Twilio delivers WhatsApp messages when that channel is connected.
    </p>

    <h2>Retention</h2>
    <p>
      The current prototype keeps state in memory on the API server. Restarting the server clears the demo conversation.
      Do not send real medical records or secrets you cannot afford to lose.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      For a production deployment you would get access, deletion, and export controls. In this prototype, clear the session
      by restarting the API or stop sending messages.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this prototype: use the project repository maintainers.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
